@startuml
!theme plain
|a_default| Default
|a_default|
start
:To initiate the process for the election of a rector, it is necessary to begin with the rector's final year in their current position.;
:the acceptance of proposals for candidates for the rector position should be launched.;
:the rector can nominate themselves as a candidate for the position.;
:the acceptance of proposals should be stopped.;
:If a candidate meets the required criteria;
:v1: Candidate meets required criteria ({true, false}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v1 = true])
:they should be included in the list of candidates.;
:Simultaneously,;
split
:it should be made public.;
split again
:the candidates should promote their ideas to the public;
split again
:organize a public meeting of the Academic Senate.;
end split
:The public meeting should then commence, ensuring that all members are able to vote for a new rector.;
:Following the meeting, an election should be conducted and the votes should be counted.;
:v2: Voting successful ({true, false}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v2 = false])
:If the voting fails;
:another election should be conducted.;
else ([v2 = true])
:the result of the election should be announced.;
:the public meeting should be concluded;
:the candidate should be informed of the election results;
:marking the end of the process.;
stop
endif
else ([v1 = false])
:they should be informed of the refusal and the process will come to an end.;
stop
endif
@enduml